Fermata's attestor (github.com/bilgin-kocak/fermata, apps/attestor) @ d7cc642, Apache License 2.0:
  - apps/attestor: prove.rs, notary.rs, tunnel.rs, http_raw.rs, predicate.rs and config.rs copied;
    verify.rs, serve.rs, main.rs and tests/attest.rs adapted; chain.rs replaced, keeping its
    ChainView trait, MockChain and JSON-RPC transport; Cargo.lock extended. Its TLSNotary code
    comes from WebProof and the upstream tlsn `attestation` example at v0.1.0-alpha.15
    (github.com/tlsnotary/tlsn, MIT or Apache-2.0).

WebProof (github.com/bilgin-kocak/webproof-solana) @ 609a654, Apache License 2.0:
  - the domain-separated claim pattern (a versioned ASCII tag followed by canonical bytes,
    signed with Ed25519, pinned by a text vector file) from crates/webproof-core/src/lib.rs
  - docs/trust-model.md: structure and wording adapted from docs/trust-model.md

Designs followed, with no code copied:
  - packages/sdk/src/hold.ts: the sponsored ("pull") flow of Stellar's MPP Charge,
    github.com/stellar/stellar-mpp-sdk @ 90394ec (MIT, as its package.json declares)
  - packages/sdk/src/mpp/session.ts: the credential shape (an `action` per credential) of the
    `channel` intent of Stellar's MPP SDK, github.com/stellar/stellar-mpp-sdk @ 90394ec
  - packages/sdk/src/x402: the escrow flow of x402's auth-capture draft and the `exact` scheme on
    Stellar, github.com/x402-foundation/x402 @ e95b066, specs/ (Apache License 2.0)
  - packages/sdk/src/channels.ts: the HTTP API of OpenZeppelin's Channels plugin,
    github.com/OpenZeppelin/relayer-plugin-channels @ c7cf073 (its package.json declares MIT, its
    LICENSE file is AGPL-3.0)
